ah snake oil the phrase is often used to  characterize grifters and con artists  but where did the same come from well  the story starts in the 1800s Chinese  immigrants working on the first  transcontinental railroad rub snake oil  on their skin to treat joint pain  Westerners eventually caught on and  marveled at its apparent healing powers  while some admired it others saw  opportunity in comes Clark rattlesnake  king Stanley he was a self-proclaimed  cowboy and so-called expert in  traditional Native American medicine  we're going to make a quick buck he  teamed up with a boston druggist and  began marketing clark Stanley's snake  oil in a miracle medicine promised to  heal your rheumatism neuralgia sciatica  blame back lembaga toothache sore throat  animal bites Gungan disease alright that  last one isn't real but who cares the  sucker would fix anything that L did  Clark took his product on the road  visiting fairs and put on elaborate  spectacles in front of a hungry crowd  during one show he squeezed the snake to  death and bottled up its residue while  some were mesmerised others were  skeptical after seeing the injustice is  made to Public Health famous muckraker  Samuel Hopkins Adams investigated the  fraudulent patent medicine industry  and wrote the watershed expose the great  American fraud this led to the federal  government seizing a shipment of the  snake oil and analyzing it they found  out that it was made mostly just mineral  oil the quack medicine industry came to  an end when the Pure Food and Drug Act  was passed the feds slapped Clark with a  $20 fine and he promptly closed up shop  so samuel exposed the frauds Clark  Stanley had the last laugh  you  [Music]
 

